I'm seeing some weird caching behavior too with playwright component tests for react, same version (`1.33.0`).  For me, removing the cache (`rm -rf ./playwright/.cache`) doesn't help, there seems to be some other caching done on the file path level.

@mikeogi  just checking, if you make a one-letter change to your directory where your code is, do the tests pass as expected?  This seems to "bust" the cache.  I'm wondering if playwright team can share some guidance on what might be cached on this file-level, and how to clear this, until a fix is deployed.  

I'm also pretty sure that this is only happening after upgrading from version `1.31.2` =>  `1.32.0`.  The diff between those versions is quite large, I was trying to see what might be causing it.
